 ],
 "text": "I always thought that I have to do it alone and I have to be fierce and I have to be strong. But really I can rely on my wound that is connected to the earth. During my first ceremony I really felt that the secret plant was helping me to repair things in myself. Especially in my wound where I was hurt a lot. And it was building me up bit by piece. Before the next ceremony, I did a kambal to really open up myself to all the plant medicine. And in the evening when I went again for the teaching of the secret plant, I felt it was more profound, more deep. And I also had a very large connection with my wound and from my wound to the earth. I felt that I belonged to this earth, that I made from this earth, that my roots are in this earth and I can trust that I'm being carried by the earth, by my ancestors and by everybody who is supporting me and my soul. I'm very grateful for that experience and I hope to inspire a lot more people, a lot of women to grow from their wounds, from their roots.",
 "language": "en"
}